# ── NIP-20: NBL-20 Fungible Token Standard ──────────────────────────
# Abstract:
#   The NBL-20 standard defines a common interface for fungible
#   tokens on the NEBULA blockchain. This is analogous to ERC-20
#   on Ethereum, enabling interoperability across DeFi protocols.
#
# Required Functions:
#   name()             → str   : Token name
#   symbol()           → str   : Token symbol
#   decimals()         → int   : Decimal places
#   total_supply()     → int   : Total token supply
#   balance_of(addr)   → int   : Balance of address
#   transfer(to, amt)  → bool  : Transfer tokens
#   approve(spender, amt) → bool : Approve spending
#   transferFrom(from, to, amt) → bool : Delegated transfer
#   allowance(owner, spender) → int : Remaining allowance
#
# Optional Functions:
#   mint(to, amount)   → bool  : Create new tokens (if mintable)
#   burn(amount)       → bool  : Destroy tokens
#   pause()            → bool  : Pause transfers (if pausable)
#   unpause()          → bool  : Resume transfers
#
# Events:
#   Transfer(from: Address, to: Address, value: uint256)
#   Approval(owner: Address, spender: Address, value: uint256)
#
# Implementation Notes:
# Use Python integers for all amounts (no float arithmetic)
# Always validate input addresses before state changes
# Check balance before transfer to prevent underflow
# Emit events for all state changes
# Consider ERC-777 hooks for receiver notification

# ── NIP-81: NBL-721 Non-Fungible Token Standard ─────────────────────
# Abstract:
#   The NBL-721 standard defines a common interface for non-fungible
#   tokens (NFTs) on NEBULA. Each token has a unique identifier and
#   can have associated metadata, royalties, and transfer restrictions.
#
# Required Functions:
#   balance_of(owner)              → int   : NFTs owned
#   owner_of(collection, token_id) → str   : Current owner
#   transfer(collection, id, to)   → bool  : Transfer NFT
#   approve(collection, id, addr)  → bool  : Approve transfer
#   get_approved(col, id)          → str   : Get approved address
#   set_approval_for_all(op, bool) → bool  : Operator approval
#   is_approved_for_all(own, op)   → bool  : Check operator
#   token_uri(collection, id)      → str   : Metadata URI
#
# Required Events:
#   Transfer(from, to, token_id)
#   Approval(owner, approved, token_id)
#   ApprovalForAll(owner, operator, approved)
#
# Royalty Interface (NIP-81 extension):
#   royalty_info(token_id, sale_price) → (recipient, amount)
#   Implements on-chain royalty enforcement
#   Maximum royalty: 15% of sale price
#
# Metadata Standard (NIP-81 JSON Schema):
#   {
#     "name":        "Collection Name #1",
#     "description": "NFT description text",
#     "image":       "ipfs://... or https://...",
#     "attributes":  [{"trait_type": "...", "value": "..."}],
#     "external_url": "https://...",
#     "animation_url": "ipfs://..."   // optional
#   }

